          "Invest in the district's professional and technology economy: the 20.98% Asian demographic and high college-attainment rate signal presence of technology workers, healthcare professionals, and research-sector employees whose economic mobility depends on regional competitiveness — advocate specifically for policies that attract talent and investment to Northern Virginia.",
          "Acknowledge and engage the 33% Republican opposition as a credible constituency: this is not a district where Democratic supermajority means dismissing opposition concerns — the 33% represents educated, affluent voters with legitimate fiscal conservatism and property-owner interests who must be governed for, not around.",
          "Avoid any positioning that treats affluence or education as a liability or that frames the district's high income as evidence of unfairness: this electorate supports progressive taxation and public investment, but they are not self-flagellating about their own success — messaging that implies their prosperity is the problem will alienate rather than energize them."
