          "Recognize that 34% renter rate in a district with $120,220 median income signals young professionals and urban service workers whose housing and education costs consume substantial portions of income despite high nominal earnings; candidates who speak to the material economic pressures of this constituency — not abstract arguments about governance — build credibility across demographic lines."
