          { name: "Cost-of-Living Sustainability for Young Professionals", tag: "careful", why: "At 36.1 median age, 23.4% renter rate, and $159,473 median income, the district is young homeowners and early-career professionals acutely aware of whether their income is keeping pace with Northern Virginia's rising costs — property taxes, childcare, healthcare. This constituency is economically conservative on fiscal management even while being socially progressive; they will evaluate a representative on whether state policy is making their economic position more or less sustainable, not only on ideology." },
          { name: "Treating 65% as an Unbreakable Democratic Floor", tag: "avoid", why: "A 65-35 result in a multiethnic district with substantial Hispanic and Asian populations is strong but contingent on active engagement of those communities' specific economic concerns. Any representative who assumes that 65% reflects stable Democratic partisanship across all cohorts rather than coalition maintenance is misreading the district; a swing of 5 percentage points among Hispanic or Asian voters would move the seat from +30 to +20 in a single cycle." },
          { name: "Ignoring the White College-Educated Constituency's Fiscal Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "The 54.2% college-attainment rate and $159,473 median income signal a professionally accomplished constituency that is politically progressive but also fiscally conservative and responsive to competence-based governance messaging. A representative who defaults to ideology-first positioning rather than demonstrating concrete fiscal management and educational quality will find this cohort — which is 40.51% of the district — becoming persuadable to a moderate Republican challenger if one emerges." }
