          { name: "Generic Racial Equity Messaging Without Economic Specificity", tag: "avoid", why: "At 49.98% Black and 9.65% Hispanic, HD-80's constituencies evaluate representation not on abstract support for racial equity but on whether their representative is creating tangible economic pathways — job access, business support, homeownership opportunity, wage growth. A representative whose positioning relies on generic racial justice rhetoric without concrete legislative work on Black and Latino economic mobility will find that the 95% margin masks underlying frustration with unmet material needs. Constituents distinguish sharply between symbolic acknowledgment and substantive economic investment in their communities." }
