          { name: "Ignoring the 16.9% Renter Population's Housing & Affordability Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "While VA-HD-89 is 83.1% homeowners, the 16.9% renter population in a district with median household income of $107,397 likely includes both service-sector workers experiencing housing cost burden and younger adults or recent arrivals unable to access homeownership despite high incomes — both constituencies with specific legislative interests in housing affordability, zoning policy, and rental protections. A representative who campaigns exclusively to homeowner interests while ignoring renters' material concerns about housing access and cost burden will leave electoral space for opposition messaging on economic fairness and generational opportunity. In a district this educated, voters recognize affordability framing as real policy, not resentment politics." }
