          "Engage the renter and younger adult constituency (31.6% renters, median age 38.5) on economic mobility and household financial security: housing affordability, education costs, healthcare expenses, and wage stagnation are the material concerns that shape how renters and younger adults evaluate their representative's effectiveness, particularly at a $72,251 median income where households feel economic pressure despite being middle-class.",
          "Build specific outreach to the Hispanic community (10.25%): economic integration concerns, healthcare access, and whether the district's governance benefits Hispanic families proportionally are tangible issues that require active constituent engagement rather than assumption of political alignment.",
          "Avoid treating 69% as a permanent floor: the combination of a 31.6% renter rate, 26.9% college attainment, and 31% Democratic opposition in a heavily Republican district signals constituencies (renters, educated adults, minorities) whose political loyalty is conditional on whether they perceive government as delivering for them — not inherited partisan identity."
