          { name: "Confusing Low College Attainment with Low Constituent Intelligence or Interest in Economic Opportunity", tag: "avoid", why: "VA-SD-9's 17.5% college-attainment rate is the lowest marker in this analysis, but it reflects the district's working-class composition and limited educational infrastructure—not constituent indifference to economic mobility or inability to recognize whether government is delivering for them. A legislator who campaigns as though a low-education-attainment constituency is satisfied with symbolic messaging rather than concrete workforce development, housing affordability, and wage-supporting policy will find that assumption actively punished by voters who evaluate on material results." }
