          "Engage the college-educated professional constituency (31.5%) directly on education policy, environmental stewardship, and the quality-of-life issues that affluent professionals use to evaluate alignment — ignoring this 30%+ of the district risks creating space for a future challenger who speaks directly to professional-class concerns.",
          "Build a legislative record that reflects suburban Virginia's material economy: transportation and commuting, broadband infrastructure, housing affordability at the professional-class level, and the regulatory environment for small business — not abstract conservative positioning, but concrete governance that serves the district's actual demographic reality.",
