          { name: "Culture War Positioning Over Fiscal & Governance Competence", tag: "avoid", why: "VA-SD-12's affluent, educated, suburban professional constituency does not vote primarily on cultural or ideological positioning — it votes on whether government is delivering fiscal responsibility, quality schools, public safety, and competent management of the services they depend on and pay for through substantial property taxes. Any candidate who emphasizes abstract conservative cultural messaging over specific answers to questions about school funding, property tax fairness, development planning, and public safety infrastructure will find themselves losing persuadable educated voters to an opponent positioned as the more credible competence choice. In this district, governance delivery beats ideology every time." }
