          { name: "Allowing Local Governance Failures to Accumulate Unchecked", tag: "avoid", why: "While the state Senate seat itself may be secure at 62%, degradation of public trust through accumulation of unaddressed constituent problems—school funding shortfalls, public safety failures, service delivery delays—creates the political environment in which a well-resourced challenger can gain traction even in a Democratic lean district. The incumbent's responsibility is not only to vote correctly in Richmond but to deliver for constituents on the ground. Allowing K-12 funding issues, neighborhood safety concerns, or other material constituent failures to fester without visible incumbent engagement is the most likely pathway to erosion of the 62% margin." }
