          "Engage Latino constituency on immigration, labor rights, and education: the 20.68% Latino population is neither assumed nor monolithic—address education access for immigrant families, labor standards enforcement for service and agricultural workers, and immigration enforcement policy with specificity rather than broad messaging. Material constituent concerns drive voting behavior in this community more than abstract party affiliation.",
          "Deliver for renters on housing policy, tenant protections, and cost-of-living relief: at 36.5% renter rate and $72,133 median income, housing affordability and tenant stability are pressing concerns for over a third of the district. A legislative record that demonstrates concrete wins on rent stabilization, renter rights, or housing supply is the most durable proof of constituent service; absence of meaningful housing policy work opens space for a challenger to argue the incumbent is not delivering.",
