          { name: "Healthcare Cost & Access for High-Income Professionals", tag: "lean-into", why: "Professional households at $99,417 median income face specific healthcare pressures: high deductibles on employer plans, childcare-related coverage gaps, and long-term care costs as parents age. These are material economic concerns for a workforce with disposable income but also significant fixed costs. A representative who addresses healthcare access and cost control through state-level policy levers — insurance regulation, provider network protections, prescription drug cost management — speaks directly to the financial pressures that affluent professionals actually experience, rather than defaulting to ideological healthcare messaging." },
          { name: "Demographic Diversity & Coalition-Building Across Racial & Ethnic Communities", tag: "careful", why: "At 59.93% white, 14.02% Black, and 13.86% Asian, VA-SD-16 is a genuinely diverse district where no single racial or ethnic cohort dominates, but where educated professionals of different backgrounds share common interests in education quality, healthcare access, and economic mobility. The 55% Democratic result suggests that this diversity has consolidated around Vanvalkenburg, but a challenger who can demonstrate specific understanding of Asian professionals' economic mobility concerns, Black professionals' educational equity priorities, and Hispanic professionals' healthcare access issues — as distinct constituencies with particular needs — has the capacity to fracture this coalition. Any incumbent must maintain active engagement with these communities as distinct groups, not absorbed into generic diversity rhetoric." },
          { name: "Treating 55% as a Durable Majority in a Wealthy, Educated, Genuinely Competitive District", tag: "avoid", why: "A 55-45 result in a district with this demographic profile is not a durable majority — it is a contested plurality among high-information voters who remain persuadable on grounds of demonstrated competence and specific policy delivery. Any incumbent who campaigns this seat as though 55% represents a safe hold rather than a working coalition of educated professionals evaluating on substance will find that coalition vulnerable to a challenger who offers more detailed policy specificity or more credible constituent attention. This district's voters have high information diets; they will reward detailed legislative work and punish generic messaging." },
          { name: "Generic Partisan Messaging in a District Where Voters Evaluate on Competence", tag: "avoid", why: "VA-SD-16's college-educated professionals have low tolerance for abstract partisan rhetoric and high demand for demonstrated policy knowledge and legislative effectiveness. Any candidate who relies on party-line messaging or ideological positioning without grounding arguments in specific Virginia state policy, constituent needs data, or detailed legislative accomplishments will struggle to persuade a constituency that is comparing candidates on competence grounds. The 55-45 margin reflects voters who are not locked into partisan alignment; they are evaluating whether their representative has the knowledge and capacity to deliver on the specifics that affect their lives." }
