          { name: "Focusing on Partisan Identity Rather than Economic Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "At 31.8 median age and 55.7% renter status, VA-SD-21 contains a substantial cohort of younger adults whose economic mobility concerns — housing affordability, wage growth, healthcare access, student debt management — are more salient than inherited partisan loyalty. A legislative agenda focused on partisan messaging, cultural signaling, or ideological positioning without concrete connection to the material economic constraints facing renters and younger adults risks losing engagement from the coalition members most susceptible to persuasion on alternative messengers. The 77% margin is real, but it masks potential fragility in a constituency whose primary leverage is economic security and opportunity rather than partisan identity." }
