          "Engage the Black community's material economic concerns specifically — not as a demographic to be thanked but as a constituency whose household economic security, healthcare access, and economic mobility require concrete policy delivery and measurable outcomes that justify the 77% support level.",
          "Recognize the 40% white opposition as a constituency worth engaging on economic and community concerns; the 77% margin depends on meaningful white support, and treating that third of the district as irretrievable alienates a potential persuasion constituency and invites a challenger to reframe the race on competence.",
          "Treat 77% as requiring active coalition maintenance, not as an insurmountable majority: the margin is real but fragile if the incumbent's agenda shifts away from the economic constraints and community priorities that create the existing Democratic base."
