          "Build explicit Black voter engagement around economic mobility, education quality, and healthcare access: the 27.43% Black population is large enough that modest changes in turnout or preference margins shift the overall result, and current 55% performance suggests either turnout risk or meaningful Republican crossover that needs direct attention.",
          "Address renter and young professional economic concerns with specificity: the 36.4% renter rate and 35.8-year median age represent a constituency for whom housing costs, student debt, and economic opportunity are primary household budget concerns — offering concrete policy remedies on these fronts is essential to holding and growing the Democratic margin.",
          "Defend against Republican gains in affluent neighborhoods and precincts: the 45% Republican result in an educated, high-income district signals effective Republican messaging on taxes and economic governance in constituencies that have material interest in those concerns — understand which neighborhoods are most competitive and build constituent relationships that counteract this messaging."
