          "Defend against suburban erosion by engaging college-educated voters on their actual concerns: transportation infrastructure connecting to Washington-area employment, school quality and funding, healthcare access and Medicare sustainability for the 45.3-year-old median age, and tax policy that protects property values — not cultural rhetoric that drives educated voters away.",
