          "Engage Hispanic voters (14% of district) and Asian voters (3.47%) as active swing constituencies, not afterthoughts: both communities in affluent suburbs evaluate on economic mobility, school quality, and whether government delivers for their families — specific constituent attention on education funding, housing affordability, and small business support builds durable support in ways generic minority outreach does not.",
          "Lead with school quality and local governance specifics: at 36.8 median age with 24.8% renters, the district is younger families evaluating on schools, property values, and whether local government is delivering — abstract partisan messaging loses to candidates who demonstrate fluency on specific school performance, infrastructure, and tax policy.",
          "Treat 52% as a competitive margin, not a secure hold: in a district where the Republican candidate held 48% of a college-educated, affluent suburban constituency, any Democratic incumbent or challenger who campaigns as though education levels and income alone guarantee Democratic votes will be vulnerable to a credible Republican challenger who addresses local governance concerns directly."
